<title>JAPAN: Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</title>
<headline>Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mikuni and Co Ltd said on Friday it had assigned the following preliminary ratings to planned bond issues:</p>
<p>-AA-</p>
<p>Kyushu Electric Power Co Inc, 350 million Swiss Francs mortgaged due 2007.</p>
<p>-A-</p>
<p>Mitsubishi Electric Corp,</p>
<p>10 billion yen unsecured due 2002,</p>
<p>20 billion yen unsecured due 2003,</p>
<p>10 billion yen unsecuerd due 2004.  </p>
<p>-BBB-</p>
<p>Rohto Pharmaceutical Co Ltd, five billion yen unsecured convertible due 2002.</p>
<p>-B-</p>
<p>Tokyo Seimitsu Co Ltd, 400 million yen unsecured with warrants due 2001.</p>
<p>Towa Corp,</p>
<p>five billion yen unsecured convertible due 2001, private placement,</p>
<p>three billion yen unsecured convertible due 2004.  </p>
<p>-B-</p>
<p>Yamatane Corp, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2003.</p>
<p>-CCC-</p>
<p>Alinco Inc,</p>
<p>40 million Swiss Francs unsecured convertible due 2001, private placement,</p>
<p>420 million yen unsecured with warrants due 2001.</p>
</text>
